# File Organization and Project Structure

## Testnet Directory
- All non-project files MUST be in `testnet/` directory
- Includes: test configs, temporary files, test node data, test logs, experimental files
- Exceptions: Source code (`app/`, `cmd/`, `x/`, `proto/`), documentation (`docs/`), config files

## Documentation Organization
- Specifications go to `docs/`: architecture, API, protocols, system design, economic model, consensus, modules, infrastructure
- All other documentation goes to `deprecated/`: deployment guides, improvement plans, user guides, status reports
- Exception: `README.md` stays in root

## Official whitepapers (do not delete)
- `docs/WHITEPAPER.md` — English whitepaper (canonical public narrative aligned with protocol specs).
- `docs/WHITEPAPER_RU.md` — Russian whitepaper (same specification version; links to English).
- **These files must not be deleted.** If the protocol evolves, **update** them in place (or add new sections); do not remove the whitepaper files from the repository. Relocation or renaming requires an explicit project decision and must preserve both language editions.
- Detailed version-by-version changelog of the specification text remains in `docs/volnix_protocol.md`; whitepapers may omit the long appendix of per-release deltas.

## Documentation Naming
- Use UPPERCASE_WITH_UNDERSCORES.md format
- Examples: `PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md`, `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md`
- Exception: `README.md` can use any case

## Infrastructure Directory
- All infrastructure files in `infrastructure/`: monitoring configs, Grafana dashboards
- Structure: `infrastructure/monitoring/`, `infrastructure/grafana/`

## Backend Directory
- All backend services and API servers go to `backend/`: REST API servers, gRPC gateways, microservices, background workers
- Structure: `backend/api/`, `backend/services/`, `backend/workers/`, `backend/utils/`
- Backend services are separate from blockchain node (`cmd/volnixd/`) and application code (`app/`)
- Examples: REST API wrapper, webhook services, indexing services, external API integrations
- Each service should have its own subdirectory with `README.md` and configuration files

## Simulation Directory
- `simulation/` is an **off-chain** protocol/economics playground: **FastAPI** backend and **Vite + React** frontend. It is **not** the Cosmos node (`cmd/volnixd/`, `app/`) and **not** the repo-wide production services tree `backend/`.
- `simulation/backend/` — HTTP/WebSocket API (`main.py`); simulation logic lives in `core/` (e.g. `engine`, `state`, `models`, `bot_engine`, wallet validation helpers).
- `simulation/frontend/` — dashboard UI; API base URL and env-specific settings via `src/config.ts` (and `vite-env.d.ts` for typings).
- Treat on-chain modules (`x/`, `proto/`) as the source of truth for consensus rules; the simulation may simplify or mirror flows for demos and tests.

## Simulation v2 Directory
- `simulation_v2/` is a **greenfield** off-chain blockchain-node simulator for canon **5.1-sim** (`simulation_v2/docs/volnix_protocol.md`). It is **not** the Cosmos node and **not** `simulation/` (v1).
- `simulation_v2/backend/` — Python FastAPI node: JSONL blockstore, ABCI-like application (canon modules), CometBFT-style RPC, explorer REST `/api/v1`, WebSocket `/ws`.
- `simulation_v2/frontend/` — explorer / dashboard (to be implemented against `/api/v1`).
- `simulation_v2/traffic/` — separate process for network traffic / economy (bot wallets, stub ZKP, transfers, market, declare). Talks to the node over HTTP operator + explorer APIs; does **not** embed into `backend/volnix/node/`. Control API default `:8002`. Env prefix: `VOLNIX_SIM2_TRAFFIC_*`.
- `simulation_v2/docs/` — working canon and API for the v2 stand.
- Runtime chain data lives in `simulation_v2/backend/data/` (gitignored via the global `data/` pattern). Genesis template is `config/genesis.default.json` (do **not** name it `genesis.json` — that filename is globally gitignored).
- Env prefix (node): `VOLNIX_SIM2_*`.

## Non-Source Files (MUST be in .gitignore)
- Check `.gitignore` BEFORE creating non-source files
- If pattern exists → safe to create, if not → add to `.gitignore` first
- Non-source categories:
  - Build artifacts: `build/`, `frontend/*/build/`, `*.exe`, `*.o`, `*.test`, `coverage/`
  - Generated code: `proto/gen/`, `.generated/`
  - Dependencies: `vendor/`, `node_modules/` (lock files like `package-lock.json` are committed per `dependencies.mdc`)
  - Test data: `testnet/`, `tmp/`, `*.log`, `*.bak`
  - Local config: `.volnix/`, `.env`, `config.toml`, `*.db`, private keys
  - IDE/OS files: `.vscode/`, `.DS_Store`, `*.swp`
  - Deprecated: `deprecated/`

## Project Structure
- Root: essential project files only
- Source code: `app/`, `cmd/`, `x/`, `proto/volnix/`, `tests/`
- Backend services: `backend/` (committed, separate services from blockchain node)
- Simulation demo: `simulation/` (v1 FastAPI + React) and `simulation_v2/` (v2 node + explorer frontend + `traffic/` economy process; separate from repo `backend/` and the Cosmos node)
- Config/scripts: `config/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, `.cursor/`
- Infrastructure: `infrastructure/` (committed, required for deployment)
- Test artifacts: `testnet/` (ignored)
- Build artifacts: `build/`, `proto/gen/` (ignored)

## .gitignore Rules
- All non-source patterns MUST be in `.gitignore` before creation
- Update both this file and `.gitignore` when adding new patterns
- Files in `.gitignore` = safe to create, files NOT in `.gitignore` = will be committed

## Best Practices
- Always check `.gitignore` before creating non-source files
- Never create non-source files not in `.gitignore`
- Keep this file and `.gitignore` synchronized
- Organize testnet files by purpose (e.g., `testnet/node0/`)
- Clean up testnet directory periodically
